method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:f448289f9bff37a016b4dd16e84e4b96b838d62ef947b70a040f0700e2ddaf56","file":"preprints/two-limit-cycles-for-quintic-lienard-systems-September-24-2026/build/sections/arcs.tex","line":498,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"711688f5ceceacf4143b3a90c8140aaf2b916c30f4dee36c5f943c580a211251","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/two-limit-cycles-for-quintic-lienard-systems-September-24-2026/build/sections/arcs.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:f448289f9bff37a016b4dd16e84e4b96b838d62ef947b70a040f0700e2ddaf56","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/two-limit-cycles-for-quintic-lienard-systems-September-24-2026/build/sections/arcs.tex#L498"},"statement_kind":"proposition","text":"\\label{prop:cycle-matching}\nFor the system\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:arc-lienard-system}\n  \\dot x=y-F(x),\\qquad \\dot y=-x,\n\\end{equation}\nthe images of nonconstant periodic solutions are in one-to-one\ncorrespondence with the zeros of\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:cycle-matching}\n  \\Delta(r)=M_+(0,r)-M_-(0,r)\n\\end{equation}\non the single open interval\n\\(\\mathcal I=\\mathcal I_+\\cap\\mathcal I_-\\).\nIf this interval is empty, there are no such periodic solutions.\nEach periodic orbit has exactly one positive and one negative\nintersection with the \\(y\\)-axis. Under the correspondence,\nisolated periodic orbits are exactly isolated zeros of \\(\\Delta\\)."}
